{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The dimension table is now fixed:\n\n| Feature | Dimensions / placement (mm) |\n|---|---|\n| Overall envelope | Ø130 × 140 long |\n| Circular flanges | Ø130, 5 thick each; top-down depths 27–32 and 135–140 |\n| Main tube | Ø70 outside; straight portion at depths 42–125 |\n| Upper neck | Ø80 at the underside of the lobed flange; R5 and R10 transitions |\n| Flange/body blends | R10, reaching Ø90 at the circular flange faces |\n| Lobed flange | 12 thick; six R10 lobes joined by concave R40 arcs; 110 across opposite tips |\n| Upper recess | Ø70 × 10 deep |\n| Circular-flange holes | 12 × Ø8 per flange, radius 55; ordinate callouts 27.50 and 47.63 |\n| Lobed-flange holes | 6 × Ø10; centers (±45, 0), (±22.50, ±38.97), giving a nominal Ø90 bolt circle |\n| Other profile checks | 87.25 between opposite scallop valleys; 64.97 reference span in Detail B |\n| Undimensioned details | 3 mm tube wall; small edge breaks inferred from the views |\n\nFor the axial chain, the **140 overall** runs from the lobed flange’s top face to the bottom flange’s bottom face. The section’s **130 component span** runs from the recess floor to that bottom face, and **10** runs from the top face to the recess floor: `140 = 10 + 130`. The **12** runs from the top face to the lobed flange underside; it is already included in 140.\n\nUsing the top face as depth zero: `140 = 12 + 15 + 5 + 10 + 83 + 10 + 5`. These are the lobed plate, neck relief, upper circular flange, upper blend, straight tube, lower blend, and bottom flange respectively. I’ll model with the bottom face at Z=0.\n"}}
